00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:07.453
One moment.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.203
Okay.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:14.410
In the morning hours
of November 8th, 1942,

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:18.090
the American and British
armies began Operation Torch.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.290
At that time, the largest
amphibious landing

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:21.980
in recorded human history,

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:25.400
the invasion saw 110,000
troops in 800 warships

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.880
and transports land on a score of beaches

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.800
spanning more than 1200
miles of the Atlantic

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.583
and Mediterranean coastlines.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.950
The key site for the
campaign was North Africa

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.000
and all involved in the strategic planning

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.380
agreed that victory ran
through the rapid seizure

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:42.843
of the city of Algiers.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.690
Now it's well known that Operation Torch

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.240
opened a crucial second
front and World War II,

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.000
soon chasing the access
forces from North Africa,

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.080
setting in motion the allied
liberation of Southern Europe.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.560
What is far less well known
is that the allied path

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.360
into Algiers was paved by the work

00:03:58.360 --> 00:03:59.700
of an underground movement,

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.420
in which a band of young Jewish liberals

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:03.990
teamed with a group of arch
conservative military brass

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:05.360
and businessmen.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.370
Over a period of months
proceeding the invasion,

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:09.970
the resisters coordinated their
efforts with the Americans

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:11.960
in particular with Robert Murphy,

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.700
the special US Envoy to the region,

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:16.770
who reported directly to
President Franklin D. Roosevelt.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.330
In the last days before the invasion,

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:21.180
the home of Henri Aboulker
became the headquarters

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.020
for the insurgency.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:24.230
Aboulker was a prominent figure

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.800
in the Algerian Jewish community

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.230
and more broadly respected
as a doctor, professor

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:29.950
and local political leader.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.320
His son who's pictured here on the left.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:35.200
The 22 year old medical
student, José Aboulker,

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.420
had been one of the earliest
to organize resistance

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.830
in Algeria and would
assume central importance

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:40.863
in the insurrection.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:43.730
In the wee hours of November 8th,

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:45.420
the designated date of the allied landing,

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:47.800
a rather motley group of
several hundred students,

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.427
shop owners, doctors, lawyers

00:04:49.427 --> 00:04:51.500
and a handful of French military officers

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.320
managed to take over nearly
all of Vichy France's

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:55.940
major institutions in Algiers

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:59.640
and they placed the regimes
key leaders under house arrest.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:02.170
The success of the underground
was all the more remarkable

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:04.400
for the numerous obstacles they faced.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.790
The insurgents were ill-equipped,

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.940
only possessing several
hundred level rifles

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.820
that predated World War
I and tour buses provided

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:11.990
by the Americans.

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:14.700
In many cases, their claim
to authority was thin.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:16.750
They had disguised themselves
by wearing armbands

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.530
with the initials VP.

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:21.200
The insignia of a local volunteer militia

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.170
tied to the Vichy Regime.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.580
In the days before the invasion,

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:26.090
promised arms from the Americans

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.920
repeatedly failed to appear.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:30.280
At the appointed time on
the night of November 8th,

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.500
at least one third of the
young men who had affiliated

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:35.470
with the insurgency
movement did not show up.

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:38.330
In the midst of chaos
José Aboulker took charge

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:40.840
as various teams of insurgents
fanned out to key points

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.040
throughout the city.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:45.150
At a series of locations in
the same scene repeated itself.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.620
A small group of resistors
showed up wearing the arm bands

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:49.750
of the local militia, carrying rifles

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:52.000
and in some cases they
did not know how to use.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.080
And showing orders for them to
relieve the Vichy commanders.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.870
Unsuspecting the officers
on duty turned over control

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:00.870
of each strategic location to
the members of the insurgency.

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:05.190
Yet as dawn broke, there was
still no sign of the Americans.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:07.470
They had elected to take
a slow and circuitous path

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.430
toward Algiers rather than the rapid one

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.090
originally promised.

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:12.920
Now Vichy had begun to fight back.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:16.530
José Aboulker utilized a
blend of ruse and inspiration

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:19.620
to rally the resistors,
imploring them over the radio

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:22.410
to hold their posts for
as long as possible.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:23.770
Eventually late that day,

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:26.290
the allies entered Algiers
and took control of the city

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:27.940
without firing a shot.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:28.890
Before too long,

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:31.140
they would control the
broader Mediterranean.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.380
At the time of the invasion,

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:36.050
North Africa was under the
control of the Vichy Government.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:38.550
Francz's authoritarian pro German regime

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:40.860
that had taken powers shortly
after the French surrendered

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.150
to the Germans in June, 1940.

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:45.230
In October, 1940 of its own accord,

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:47.820
Vichy had abrogated the Crémieux Decree.

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:50.970
The act that in 1870 had
made nearly all Algerian Jews

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.920
into equal French citizens.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:54.230
The decree had been a turning point

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:55.810
in Algerian Jewish history.

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:58.010
Separating Jews from their
Muslim fellow natives,

00:06:58.010 --> 00:06:59.650
who did not enjoy citizenship

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:03.060
and became racially defined
as so-called indigène,

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:04.640
which translated to natives,

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:07.930
but had a more negative connotation.

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:10.450
And this began a process
whereby Algiers Jews

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.320
would gradually become deeply attached

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:14.260
to French language and culture.

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:17.770
Now in October of 1940,
with a stroke of a pen,

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:20.170
Jews were suddenly demoted to indigène

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.260
or colonial subjects themselves.

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:24.700
They occupied the same status as Muslims.

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:27.520
Further anti-semitic measures followed.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:30.190
Less to the consternation
of the Jewish insurgence

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:32.380
of November 8th, 1942,

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:34.090
the liberation of Algeria by the allies

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:37.230
did not restore Jews
pre-war status overnight.

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:38.730
Instead, a new battle began

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:40.760
over the territory's French leadership

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.980
and ideological direction.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:44.960
Jews despite their central
role in the uprising

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:47.860
did not succeed immediately
in regaining their rights.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:49.700
For the first few months,
following the landing,

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:51.490
all of the racial laws remained in place

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.900
and Jews who had lost
their professional position

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:55.580
or their property only recovered them

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:57.260
on an individual basis.

00:07:57.260 --> 00:08:01.100
It was only in October of
1943, nearly a year later,

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:04.153
that Jews in Algeria regained
their French citizenship.

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:07.790
Now scholarship on the Algiers underground

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:11.050
and its Jewish participants
remains rather limited.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:14.120
And today it has generally
focused on either the military

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:16.677
and political strategy of
the North African campaign

00:08:16.677 --> 00:08:18.640
and its aftermath,

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:21.330
or on the episode as a
case of Jewish heroism

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:23.500
soon betrayed by the American invaders

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:25.420
and the French administration.

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:27.300
These analyses have left
us with little sense

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:30.140
of who the resistors were
and what motivated them.

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:32.050
More specifically, we are left to wonder

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:35.580
at the curious Alliance
at the heart of the story.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:39.040
For the groups ideological
diversity was remarkable.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:41.930
Monarchists and communists,
opponents of democracy

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:44.490
and argued Republicans and
perhaps most strikingly,

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:47.520
Jews and anti-semites joined
together in what became known

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:49.350
as the movement of November 8th.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:52.330
How was this possible in the
book I'm currently writing,

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:55.260
this is among the puzzles
I'm trying to piece together.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:58.110
And the focus of much of my
talk today will be outlining

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:00.400
the participants in this rebel Alliance

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.390
and discussing some of
the possible catalysts

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:03.750
for their cooperation,

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:06.210
that not only seems
counterintuitive today,

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:08.230
but did at the time as well.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:11.660
I should add that this is
very much a book in progress,

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:14.410
and I look forward to your
questions and comments

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:16.820
as I continue to think about the issues

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.120
that I'm discussing today.

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:20.890
But before I get to this puzzle,

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:23.190
we can only appreciate the
history and significance

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:24.300
of the Algiers insurrection

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:26.940
by placing it within the
broader context of a Holocaust

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:30.093
in North Africa and European
political culture in Algeria.

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:33.740
Well, Central and Eastern Europe
of course saw the greatest

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:35.900
anti-semitic atrocities
during the Holocaust.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:37.750
The nearly half million Jews
living in French North Africa

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:39.720
suffered significantly as well.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.640
Many racial laws enacted by
Vichy were extended to Algeria,

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:44.070
Morocco and Tunisia.

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:45.730
Leading to severe professional quotas,

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:48.660
intensive surveillance, and
more than 100 labor camps.

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:50.510
Where Jewish prisoners
were often singled out

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:52.370
for especially harsh treatment.

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:56.020
Algeria is particularly
significant to the European story.

00:09:56.020 --> 00:09:58.960
The territory was in large
part and next to France

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:00.390
since the 19th century.

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:03.660
And was home to almost a million
European colonial settlers

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:06.370
whose political culture was
steeped in the anti-semitism

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.050
of the 1930s.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:11.700
By late 1941, most, excuse me,

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:13.500
most Jewish children had been expelled

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.450
from the public primary
schools in Algeria,

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:17.410
most notable and devastating

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:19.240
of the measures taken in Algeria however,

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:21.710
was Vichy's decision in autumn 1940

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:24.180
to strip all Jews of
the French citizenship

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.173
that they had enjoyed for 70 years.

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:29.940
The story of the resistance
also looks different

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.170
from the Mediterraneans Southern shore.

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:34.080
What we mostly know about
the French resistance

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:36.160
is a classic case in which
history has been written

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:37.290
by the victors.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:40.150
The wartime triumph and
post-war legacy of the galists

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:42.700
and communists, helped
to create a narrative

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:44.500
that makes several assumptions.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.870
First, we imagined that
French insurgents emerged

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:48.820
in opposition, not only to the Germans,

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:50.620
but also to the Vichy government.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:53.120
In addition, we see the resistance
is comprised of liberals,

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:55.950
Republicans, socialists, and communists.

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:58.540
Finally, according to a
stubbornly enduring narrative,

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:01.900
on one side stood Lezi
staunt fighting virtuously

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:04.510
against Nazi and Vichy anti-Semitism.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:07.130
While on the other side, stood
anti-semitic perpetrators

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:08.590
and collaborators.

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:11.410
The story of the Algiers
insurgency problematizes

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:12.823
each of these assumptions.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:17.090
The developments that would
become the Algiers insurrection

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:20.210
gathered steam across three
geographical nodal points.

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:22.560
And the first of these was not Algiers,

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:26.320
but somewhat surprisingly,
it was actually Vichy.

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:28.600
The resort town in the
Massif Central region

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:31.050
of Southern France, where
Marshal Philippe Pétain,

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:33.750
set up the new French government
after the fall of France

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.600
in June, 1940.

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:37.690
As many of you know,
Vichy was authoritarian,

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:40.430
anti-republican,
traditionalist, pro-German

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:41.880
and anti-Semitic.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:45.130
It was also as
counterintuitive as it seems,

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:48.020
an important wellspring
of early resistance.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.220
While they remain little known,

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:51.330
during the early months
following the defeat,

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:54.640
numerous Vichy officials in a double game.

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:56.640
They remained loyal to Marshal Pétain,

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:58.850
but they mistakenly believed
that he was hamstrung

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:00.040
by the occupiers

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:02.370
and that they should
thus begin to undertake

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:05.760
the work of resistance that
he ultimately supported,

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:08.993
but could not do himself and
might openly join some day.

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:12.520
These were among the group
that a handful of historians

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:15.310
of the occupation in France
have in recent years dubbed

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:17.053
vichysto-résistant.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.620
The notion of the vichysto-résistant
only really emerged

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:24.580
in the aftermath of
revelations in the mid 1990s,

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:27.620
that then French president,
François Mitterrand

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:29.380
pictured second from
the right in the photo

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:31.120
on the left here,

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:33.960
had affiliated for several
years with the organizations

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:35.170
of the far right.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:38.033
And had worked loyally for
Vichy France until 1943.

00:12:38.033 --> 00:12:43.033
This was a major shocking
scandal at the time in France.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:46.090
Indeed, the vichysto-resistant
also included many,

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:48.780
like Mitterrand who underwent
a process of evolution

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:49.970
in the course of the war.

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:52.410
From Vichy loyalists to full participants

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:53.930
in the organized resistance.

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.250
The term applies as well to
those who had been members

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.710
of interwar extreme right groups,

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:00.480
but decided or retaining their ideology

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:02.500
to act against not only the Nazis,

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:04.520
but also the Vichy regime.

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:06.530
Even as they fiercely opposed the Germans

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:09.240
and sought to renew the
French fight against Nazi-ism,

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:11.060
these men and women often supported

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:15.130
much of Vichy social policy,
including regarding Jews.

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:17.310
And this was the case for several actors

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:18.793
in the Algiers insurgency.

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:21.730
In order to account for the importance

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:25.670
of the arch conservatives, who
were the vichysto-resistant

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:28.150
and played a leading
role on the insurrection.

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:31.350
We have to turn to the second
geographic note in our story,

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:32.183
Washington.

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:35.100
Washington's eyes and ears in North Africa

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:38.130
were substantially those
of US Envoy, Robert Murphy.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:41.880
Who reported directly to
president Franklin D. Roosevelt.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:44.730
From the moment of the
French defeat in June, 1940,

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:47.560
the race was on to find partners
in French, North Africa,

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:49.610
who might play a role
in an eventual effort

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:51.060
to liberate Europe.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:53.190
Murphy along with other
key American officials,

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.770
took a decidedly pragmatic
approach in looking

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.370
for these partners.

00:13:57.370 --> 00:13:59.030
Murphy and his colleagues long believed

00:13:59.030 --> 00:14:00.910
that some version of Vichy in fact,

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:04.190
might be part of the solution
rather than the problem.

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:06.810
Eventually, the Americans became convinced

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:10.880
that General Henri Giraud
rather than Charles de Gaulle,

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:13.140
the leader of Free France in London

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:15.820
was the right man to lead the resistance.

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:18.100
Giraud was at heart,
a proud French Patriot

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:20.090
who believed the Germans
could be defeated.

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:23.270
What he sought to overturn
was not Vichy social policies,

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:26.260
but rather its decision to
collaborate with the Germans.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:29.000
Giraud himself was
unabashedly anti-semitic.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.970
The choice of Giraud as
leader of the resistance

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:32.800
highlights what would become a key pattern

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:35.010
of American conduct in North Africa.

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:37.260
A single-minded focus on winning the war

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:39.930
at the expense of
ideological considerations

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:43.170
or deep concern for Algeria Jews.

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:44.200
Giraud stepped into a movement

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:46.540
where other prominent
Frenchmen from the mainland

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:47.990
were also in key roles,

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:50.540
many of whom were equally
or more conservative.

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:52.280
This was particularly
true of the so-called

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:54.990
Committee of Five, the
group of French businessmen

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:57.550
and officers who work
closely with the insurgence

00:14:57.550 --> 00:15:01.270
and the Americans and coordinated
many of their efforts.

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:04.410
The group included Henri
d'Astier de La Vigerie.

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:06.570
A committed monarchist and longtime member

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:09.260
of the Action Française,

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:12.680
immensely influential
neo-monarchist, anti-democratic

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.590
ultranationalist political party,

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:16.410
for which a virulent anti-semitism

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:19.540
was a central preoccupation,
since its founding

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.370
during the Dreyfus Affair.

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:24.970
d'Astier was rumored to have
participated in the Cagoule

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:27.380
of 1936 to 1937.

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:29.220
The Cagoule was originally a breakaway

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:30.090
from Action Française.

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:34.280
It was an extreme right
underground revolutionary movement,

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:38.450
whose long list of about enemies
and targets included Jews.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.460
Working close to with Italian fascists,

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:43.920
the Cagoule stockpiled weapons,
assassinated the leftists

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:47.290
and planned a coup d'etat
against the full population.

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:49.396
Two other members of
the committee of five,

00:15:49.396 --> 00:15:51.820
Jean Rigault and Jacques
Lemaigre-Dubreuil,

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:54.385
were confirmed former Cagoulel.

00:15:54.385 --> 00:15:56.620
Rigault used his closeness
to the Vichy regime

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:58.750
to foster contacts
between certain officials

00:15:58.750 --> 00:15:59.900
and the movement and Algiers.

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:03.480
Lemaigre-Dubreuil admired
Vichy's anti-democratic

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:06.500
autocratic tendencies
and its arch conservative

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:09.540
national revolution program
of national renewal.

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:12.320
And he was deeply suspicious of communism.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:14.810
Both were avowedly anti Gaullist.

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:17.970
A fourth member of the
committee, Colonel A.S. Van Hecke

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:20.253
actually headed the
Chantiers de la jeunesse,

00:16:20.253 --> 00:16:22.300
Vichy's officials scouting organization

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:24.460
meant in large part to
serve as a youth movement

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.700
that would acquire and
help to spread the values

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:28.330
of the national revolution.

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:30.366
Van Hecke sought to rally several hundreds

00:16:30.366 --> 00:16:33.090
Chantiers troops within
the Algiers underground

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:35.550
as the work of Daniel
Lee has shown recently,

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:38.980
the Chantier in the mainland
did for a time offer protection

00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:41.080
to a significant number of Jews.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:44.540
Nonetheless, in November,
1941 in administerial memo,

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:47.320
Van Hecke made no bones about
the fact that he thought

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:49.750
the Chantier in North
Africa should not accept

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:51.310
any Jewish members at all,

00:16:51.310 --> 00:16:53.540
because Jews he claimed could not acquire

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:57.180
the nationalistic values
of the national revolution.

00:16:57.180 --> 00:16:59.410
It is a memoir of the early
years of the resistance,

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:01.849
Jacques Tarbe would claim about Rigault

00:17:01.849 --> 00:17:03.380
and Lemaigre-Dubreuil.

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:04.244
And this might be said about a number

00:17:04.244 --> 00:17:06.314
of the Vichysto-resistant quote.

00:17:06.314 --> 00:17:09.680
The hostility toward
Germany was matched by their

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:11.720
hostility toward Free France.

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:14.510
A quote Free Vichy was not a free France,

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:16.480
but rather the national revolution freed

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:19.900
from the Hitlerian shackles
and protected by Washington.

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:23.610
This is what they wanted, and
this is what they almost got.

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:26.540
So Estelle's caustic remark
hinted at a deeper truth

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:28.030
that we can better appreciate

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:29.500
in light of the current scholarship

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:31.320
on the Vichysto-resistant.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:34.510
A key contingent of the
insurgency comprised men who

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:36.420
even as they took great risks and joined

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:39.410
clandestine networks to resume
the fight against the Germans

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:42.317
also had links to Vichy
that continued to influence

00:17:42.317 --> 00:17:43.513
the resistance war.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:48.100
Now, the successful turn
of the Vichysto-resistant

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:50.760
would not have been possible
after their unlikely alliance

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:53.430
with a scrappy group of Algeria Jews.

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:56.300
These Jews emerged from what
I have described elsewhere,

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:58.780
borrowing the terminology of David Sorkin

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:01.510
as an Algerian Jewish subculture

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:04.890
in the wider European sector
of Algerian colonial society.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.770
That is even as these Jews took
French first names in public

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.860
spoke primarily French in public,

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:12.530
often saw themselves as
unqualifiably French,

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:14.000
their primary community was made up

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:17.250
of other Algerian Jewish
individuals, groups

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:18.430
and institutions.

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:20.880
This was reflected in a number
of common characteristics

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:22.380
of the Jews in the insurgency.

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:26.270
Taking us into the third
noble point in our story.

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:28.540
These Jews tended to cluster
in certain neighborhoods

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:31.830
of Algiers with high
concentrations of Jews.

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:33.850
We see a marked on this map,

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:36.770
a few of those places in Algiers,

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:39.803
as well as scenes from those
neighborhoods on the left.

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:43.650
Moreover in many cases,
large numbers of resistors

00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:46.020
hailed from the same extended family.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:47.980
Among the Aboulker family for example,

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:51.780
some 15 siblings, cousins
and uncles across two cities

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:53.740
took part in the insurgency.

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:56.090
Beyond social geography
and kinship networks,

00:18:56.090 --> 00:18:59.390
a high percentage of these
Jews came from families

00:18:59.390 --> 00:19:02.290
that were active in major
Jewish organizations,

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:04.930
particularly those that
sought to fight anti-semitism

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:06.270
and improve relations

00:19:06.270 --> 00:19:08.610
with the Muslim and Christian populations.

00:19:08.610 --> 00:19:11.250
These included the major
community political organization,

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:13.620
the Algerian Jewish
Committee of Social Studies,

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:16.870
or the CJAES and the Algerian branch

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:19.570
of the largest French
anti-racist organization,

00:19:19.570 --> 00:19:22.350
the International League Against
Racism and Anti-Semitism,

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:24.450
better known as the LICRA.

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:28.250
The organizational mission of
both the CJAES and the LICRA

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:30.020
made them logical entry points

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:32.910
from which to move into active
resistance during the war.

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:36.580
The CJAES defined its
goal as keeping vigil

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:39.260
in order the Jews free
exercise of the rights

00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:42.780
of the citizen, neither be
violated nor little note.

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:44.930
The LICRA was an organization
founded precisely

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:48.250
to combat antisemitism and
whose functions by the mid 1930s

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:50.770
included that of having
certain members act

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:52.890
as a Jewish defense force.

00:19:52.890 --> 00:19:57.246
Shortly after Vichy
dissolved the LICRA in 1940,

00:19:57.246 --> 00:20:00.580
José Aboulker's cousin Rafael
pictured here on the left,

00:20:00.580 --> 00:20:02.950
who had begun attending the LICRA meetings

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:04.810
a few months earlier in Algiers,

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:07.130
gathered dispersed members
of the organization

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:09.470
and directed them toward the newly formed

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:11.880
so-called Geo Gras Group.

00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:14.070
Among the founders of the Geo Gras Group,

00:20:14.070 --> 00:20:16.220
were Emile Atlan and Andre Temime,

00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:19.413
both former activists in
the recently banned LICRA.

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:23.540
In my research, I've identified
as many as three dozen

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:27.120
former LICRA activists who
participated in the insurrection.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:29.660
Other examples of the active
Jewishness of participants

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:31.970
included charity, the local
Jewish aid organizations

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:33.840
or schools in the years before the war

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:35.430
and the several Jews in the underground

00:20:35.430 --> 00:20:38.870
who also had a role in
creating a newly self-reliant

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:40.820
Jewish school system in the face

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:42.403
of Vichy's anti-semitic laws.

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:45.610
Being active in an
organizations like the LICRA

00:20:45.610 --> 00:20:47.900
reflected another common element

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:49.950
of the Jews in the insurgency.

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:52.790
The newly aggressive politics
that defined the actions

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:54.760
and outlook of many of them.

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:58.440
One of the characteristics of
a new generation coming of age

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:01.560
in the 1930s, which highlights again,

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:04.600
the paradoxical nature of
the Wartime Rebel Alliance,

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:07.160
was widespread activist, excuse me,

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:10.130
widespread activism in
anti-fascist politics.

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:13.290
So this is extremely
common for many of those

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:15.890
who took leading roles in the insurgency.

00:21:15.890 --> 00:21:19.820
Particularly in the era after
the 1934 Constantine riots,

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:21.890
a new generation of
Algerian Jews joined groups

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:24.290
like the LICRA and became
active in large numbers

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:26.250
in the Algerian Communist Party.

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:28.380
And this marked the
beginnings of the key shift,

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:30.270
unlike much of the community establishment

00:21:30.270 --> 00:21:31.820
of their parents generation,

00:21:31.820 --> 00:21:34.440
these Jews took a more
confrontational pose,

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:37.260
gathering arms, standing up
to fascists in the street

00:21:37.260 --> 00:21:39.650
and even preemptively
attacking on occasion.

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:42.030
And the clearest echo of
this newly aggressive posture

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:43.790
within the resistance appeared

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:46.010
in the Geo Gras self-defense group,

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:47.650
that formed it autumn 1940.

00:21:47.650 --> 00:21:50.930
And that would supply in
time 130 of the insurgents

00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:52.970
who fought on November 8th.

00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:55.410
You see pictured here the boxer Geo Gras,

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:56.970
for whom the group was named.

00:21:56.970 --> 00:22:00.050
He agreed to open this space,

00:22:00.050 --> 00:22:02.380
only thinking that it was a space for

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:04.120
physical fitness and training,

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:09.060
whereas secretly this militia
was preparing itself there.

00:22:09.060 --> 00:22:11.620
And became a training round
for Jewish shock troops

00:22:11.620 --> 00:22:13.360
who would both prepare
to fight against Hitler

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:14.960
and to defend Jews.

00:22:14.960 --> 00:22:18.590
And its ranks included 80 so-called Tufts,

00:22:18.590 --> 00:22:20.500
described by resistor Lucien Adés

00:22:20.500 --> 00:22:22.630
as muscular daring fighters.

00:22:22.630 --> 00:22:24.150
They were ready at a moment's notice

00:22:24.150 --> 00:22:27.883
to confront the local militias
that regularly attacked Jews.

00:22:28.983 --> 00:22:31.980
New aspirants to the Geo Gras
Group were closely screened.

00:22:31.980 --> 00:22:35.090
If accepted, they then took
an oath to fight to the death

00:22:35.090 --> 00:22:37.680
for the liberation of France
and the defeat of the Germans

00:22:37.680 --> 00:22:40.910
and specifically to defend Algerian Jews.

00:22:40.910 --> 00:22:43.690
And there was a sense of
this generational shift

00:22:43.690 --> 00:22:47.900
that was present for Henri
Aboulker, father of José,

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:51.510
who would agree to let his
home be the headquarters

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:55.220
for the resistance in the
weeks before the landing,

00:22:55.220 --> 00:22:57.970
when he recounted later the story.

00:22:57.970 --> 00:23:01.130
And he spoke about the activism of José

00:23:01.130 --> 00:23:03.090
and his sister Colette.

00:23:03.090 --> 00:23:04.420
Ultimately he explained

00:23:04.420 --> 00:23:07.410
he had agreed to let them
use his home as a hub,

00:23:07.410 --> 00:23:09.560
mostly because he feared for their safety

00:23:09.560 --> 00:23:12.020
and sought to protect
them as any father would.

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:13.823
But he also admired them.

00:23:14.930 --> 00:23:16.280
Put the quote here.

00:23:16.280 --> 00:23:18.557
He said, "They received
no outside material help,

00:23:18.557 --> 00:23:19.557
"absolutely none,

00:23:19.557 --> 00:23:21.727
"and they all make great
personal sacrifices.

00:23:21.727 --> 00:23:25.137
"At various times, I tried to
reimburse them, they refused,

00:23:25.137 --> 00:23:27.247
"I insisted, they became angry.

00:23:27.247 --> 00:23:28.797
"Having seen all of that up close,

00:23:28.797 --> 00:23:30.357
"I loved them all the more.

00:23:30.357 --> 00:23:32.447
"I was disgusted at the general passivity,

00:23:32.447 --> 00:23:35.207
"the universal spinelessness
I had seen for years,

00:23:35.207 --> 00:23:36.717
"above all, since the defeat.

00:23:36.717 --> 00:23:39.047
"If I had died in 1940 or 1941,

00:23:39.047 --> 00:23:40.747
"I would have died in despair.

00:23:40.747 --> 00:23:43.197
"Having seen the work of
the boys of November 8th,

00:23:43.197 --> 00:23:45.277
"I was relieved. I could die in peace.

00:23:45.277 --> 00:23:47.257
"They furnished explosive proof

00:23:47.257 --> 00:23:49.097
"that pessimism should be set aside,

00:23:49.097 --> 00:23:50.957
"that there reside in our youth resources

00:23:50.957 --> 00:23:53.627
"that are unexpected, immense, unlimited."

00:23:55.470 --> 00:23:58.210
This generation's newly
assertive, left wing politics,

00:23:58.210 --> 00:24:01.720
hardly aligned, I think
that's an understatement,

00:24:01.720 --> 00:24:04.200
with those of the Vichysto-resistant,

00:24:04.200 --> 00:24:08.040
that were of course connected
very much to the right,

00:24:08.040 --> 00:24:10.790
yet with whom they
conspired in the insurgency.

00:24:10.790 --> 00:24:14.210
And indeed José Aboulker and
Henri d'Astier de La Vigerie

00:24:14.210 --> 00:24:17.080
understood that their Alliance
based on disparate goals

00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:18.500
could only be possible,

00:24:18.500 --> 00:24:20.500
if the movement reached a formal agreement

00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:22.390
to avoid politics altogether,

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:24.290
while pursuing its common ends.

00:24:24.290 --> 00:24:28.500
The two men did just
that in summer of 1942.

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:30.090
With the understanding that each group

00:24:30.090 --> 00:24:32.620
would immediately regain its
freedom of political action,

00:24:32.620 --> 00:24:35.370
following a successful allied landing.

00:24:35.370 --> 00:24:38.290
Once again, this extreme
mixture of strange bedfellows

00:24:38.290 --> 00:24:41.220
and pragmatism defies
and during assumptions

00:24:41.220 --> 00:24:43.570
about the ideological
stakes of both Jewish

00:24:43.570 --> 00:24:45.080
and non-Jewish resistance.

00:24:45.080 --> 00:24:46.890
I'm gonna stop sharing my screen now

00:24:46.890 --> 00:24:50.593
because those are at the
end of my PowerPoint images.

00:24:52.230 --> 00:24:54.420
So what was it that made such an alliance

00:24:54.420 --> 00:24:56.560
however fleeting possible?

00:24:56.560 --> 00:24:59.160
Contemporary political alignments
and historical precedents

00:24:59.160 --> 00:25:01.200
weighed heavily against it.

00:25:01.200 --> 00:25:03.000
At the heart of the
alliance was a relationship

00:25:03.000 --> 00:25:06.040
between two men who seemed
to have a little in common.

00:25:06.040 --> 00:25:07.713
The young Jewish
anti-fascist from Algiers,

00:25:07.713 --> 00:25:11.020
José Aboulker and the middle
aged French monarchist

00:25:11.020 --> 00:25:13.060
Henri d'Astier de La Vigerie.

00:25:13.060 --> 00:25:15.000
55 years later in an interview,

00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:17.267
Aboulker would put it this way, quote.

00:25:17.267 --> 00:25:19.017
"We knew that he was a monarchist

00:25:19.017 --> 00:25:21.840
"and even probably a Camelots du roi."

00:25:21.840 --> 00:25:23.610
And he referred here to this so-called

00:25:23.610 --> 00:25:26.180
Kings Camelot's youth organization

00:25:26.180 --> 00:25:29.650
of the Action Française that
frequently engaged in protests

00:25:29.650 --> 00:25:32.083
and violence street
altercations in the 1930s.

00:25:32.931 --> 00:25:34.297
Aboulker continued,

00:25:34.297 --> 00:25:36.377
"Why did I reach an
understanding with him?

00:25:36.377 --> 00:25:39.237
"Me a Jew 22 years old and anti-fascist.

00:25:39.237 --> 00:25:42.157
"This man had probably
cried death to the Jews

00:25:42.157 --> 00:25:44.917
"during protests in the
Latin quarter in Paris."

00:25:45.960 --> 00:25:48.630
His comment alluded to
the way that numerous Jews

00:25:48.630 --> 00:25:50.830
on one side and arch
conservatives on the other,

00:25:50.830 --> 00:25:52.510
had been active in opposing camps

00:25:52.510 --> 00:25:55.470
and the pitched ideological
struggles of the 1930s.

00:25:55.470 --> 00:25:58.010
But it also hearkened
back to a longer history

00:25:58.010 --> 00:26:00.880
wherein Jews and monarchists
had hardly mixed well

00:26:00.880 --> 00:26:02.380
in modern French history.

00:26:02.380 --> 00:26:03.727
As Maurice Samuel's new book,

00:26:03.727 --> 00:26:05.820
"The Betrayal of the
Duchess" shows in fact,

00:26:05.820 --> 00:26:07.850
tensions between monarchists
and Jews were crucial

00:26:07.850 --> 00:26:10.350
to the origins of modern
French anti-semitism.

00:26:10.350 --> 00:26:11.710
During the 1832 uprising

00:26:11.710 --> 00:26:13.350
of the so-called Bourbon Legitimists,

00:26:13.350 --> 00:26:14.950
that sought to reclaim the throne

00:26:14.950 --> 00:26:16.850
from the more modern old and East branch,

00:26:16.850 --> 00:26:19.170
Simon Deutz, son of the
chief rabbi of France

00:26:19.170 --> 00:26:22.290
and recent convert to
Catholicism played a key role.

00:26:22.290 --> 00:26:24.930
First Deutz gained the confidence
of the uprisings leader,

00:26:24.930 --> 00:26:26.160
the duchesse de Berry

00:26:26.160 --> 00:26:28.890
and then in exchange for a large reward

00:26:28.890 --> 00:26:31.740
from the French government,
he betrayed her.

00:26:31.740 --> 00:26:35.330
Deutz rapidly became dubbed
quote "A second Judas."

00:26:35.330 --> 00:26:37.520
And was seen as the very
embodiment of all the evils

00:26:37.520 --> 00:26:40.100
of modernism that the
legitimists and their supporters

00:26:40.100 --> 00:26:42.060
so desperately opposed.

00:26:42.060 --> 00:26:43.046
More recently in the late 19th century,

00:26:43.046 --> 00:26:46.570
Antoine Mayal, a wealthy
Jewish capitalist,

00:26:46.570 --> 00:26:47.504
had directed the right wing
royalist newspaper, Le galhua.

00:26:47.504 --> 00:26:48.337
Eventually becoming an
ardent anti-Dreyfusards,

00:26:48.337 --> 00:26:49.170
converting to Catholicism

00:26:49.170 --> 00:26:54.170
and marrying a woman of noble
origin at the age of 60.

00:26:56.370 --> 00:26:59.380
Mayal was heavily criticized
by Jewish activists

00:26:59.380 --> 00:27:01.890
like Benla Lasalle for
betraying his origins

00:27:01.890 --> 00:27:04.023
and exploiting the working class.

00:27:05.110 --> 00:27:08.850
So there was a great deal
of baggage, if you will,

00:27:08.850 --> 00:27:12.400
weighing down the possibility
of close cooperation

00:27:12.400 --> 00:27:16.700
between an ardent monarchist
and a visible Jew.

00:27:16.700 --> 00:27:18.380
And yet a series of considerations,

00:27:18.380 --> 00:27:21.020
both practical and
ideological brought together

00:27:21.020 --> 00:27:24.720
Aboulker and d'Astier and by
extension many around them.

00:27:24.720 --> 00:27:27.470
On the pragmatic side, we have
seen the US State Department

00:27:27.470 --> 00:27:30.300
decided to set aside concerns
about policy and rights

00:27:30.300 --> 00:27:33.900
in the short term, in order to
prioritize military victory.

00:27:33.900 --> 00:27:35.590
This meant supporting what became

00:27:35.590 --> 00:27:39.010
a coalition of conservative,
even anti-semitic forces

00:27:39.010 --> 00:27:40.180
and Jewish activists,

00:27:40.180 --> 00:27:42.810
since both groups were
ready to help pave the way

00:27:42.810 --> 00:27:45.040
for the Anglo-American landing.

00:27:45.040 --> 00:27:48.330
Algerian Jews meanwhile had
already in the interwar years,

00:27:48.330 --> 00:27:50.860
particularly after the
murderous Constantine riots

00:27:50.860 --> 00:27:55.610
of August, 1934, ceased
to rely as they long had

00:27:55.610 --> 00:27:58.513
on the French government
to protect their position.

00:27:59.410 --> 00:28:02.770
In an exception, Joseph Harmir
Shami's well-known argument

00:28:02.770 --> 00:28:04.740
about modern Jewish politics,

00:28:04.740 --> 00:28:07.830
they had moved increasingly
from, to use his terms,

00:28:07.830 --> 00:28:10.860
vertical to horizontal alliances.

00:28:10.860 --> 00:28:13.660
In the 1930s, these were
largely with reformists

00:28:13.660 --> 00:28:15.150
and Muslims on the left.

00:28:15.150 --> 00:28:17.900
But after the shattering events of 1940,

00:28:17.900 --> 00:28:21.050
the same Jews were equally
prepared to team with forces

00:28:21.050 --> 00:28:24.670
on the right in a temporary
alliance against a common foe.

00:28:24.670 --> 00:28:26.600
Likewise, in his memoir of the insurgency,

00:28:26.600 --> 00:28:29.830
José Aboulker himself
points out the military,

00:28:29.830 --> 00:28:31.920
that military and business leaders

00:28:31.920 --> 00:28:36.040
looking for a band of rebels
had limited options in Algiers

00:28:36.040 --> 00:28:37.620
in the 1940s.

00:28:37.620 --> 00:28:39.170
Here, unlike in France,

00:28:39.170 --> 00:28:41.800
where Jews were a tiny
percentage of the population,

00:28:41.800 --> 00:28:45.040
Jews made up 10% of the French citizens.

00:28:45.040 --> 00:28:48.340
Moreover, insists Aboulker
for those looking for allies

00:28:48.340 --> 00:28:49.470
to fight the Germans,

00:28:49.470 --> 00:28:53.880
Jews particular motivations
made them the surest bet.

00:28:53.880 --> 00:28:56.070
As historian Joanna Bahaj has argued,

00:28:56.070 --> 00:28:59.190
political flexibility was
more broadly a hallmark

00:28:59.190 --> 00:29:00.373
of the Vichysto-resistant.

00:29:01.320 --> 00:29:05.060
By 1943, notes Bahaj, despite
their fierce anti-communism,

00:29:05.060 --> 00:29:08.150
for instance, they had decided
to work alongside communists

00:29:08.150 --> 00:29:09.460
in order to be accepted

00:29:09.460 --> 00:29:11.570
within the broader French resistance.

00:29:11.570 --> 00:29:14.100
The instruction of Algiers
shows that their pragmatism

00:29:14.100 --> 00:29:17.010
in fact, dated from
earlier and extended even

00:29:17.010 --> 00:29:19.180
to an Alliance with Jews.

00:29:19.180 --> 00:29:21.790
Ideological considerations
though, were also important.

00:29:21.790 --> 00:29:25.140
Aboulker's supposition about
d'Astier's participation

00:29:25.140 --> 00:29:27.820
in anti-semitic rallies, not withstanding,

00:29:27.820 --> 00:29:31.910
d'Astier's brand of monarchism
took a more moderate position

00:29:31.910 --> 00:29:33.220
on Jews.

00:29:33.220 --> 00:29:35.460
He came from a family that
had supported the monarchy

00:29:35.460 --> 00:29:36.930
for generations.

00:29:36.930 --> 00:29:39.710
And while he retained
sympathy for the more radical

00:29:39.710 --> 00:29:43.930
neo-monarchism of Shalnohra
into the late 1930s,

00:29:43.930 --> 00:29:48.620
he was more closely aligned
with de León, Le comte de Paris,

00:29:48.620 --> 00:29:52.140
and the primary pretender at
this time to the Royal throne.

00:29:52.140 --> 00:29:54.070
In fact, in the days after
the American landing,

00:29:54.070 --> 00:29:56.810
d'Astier even helped to bring to Algiers,

00:29:56.810 --> 00:29:58.290
where he hold them up in his apartment,

00:29:58.290 --> 00:30:01.170
as he sought to negotiate
a monarchaic restoration.

00:30:01.170 --> 00:30:02.690
American general, Dwight Eisenhower,

00:30:02.690 --> 00:30:05.240
quickly quashed this idea.

00:30:05.240 --> 00:30:07.380
Le comte de Paris had repeatedly condemned

00:30:07.380 --> 00:30:09.480
the Action française in the 1930s

00:30:09.480 --> 00:30:13.120
and sought to create an
alternative strand of royalism.

00:30:13.120 --> 00:30:15.810
In January, 1939, he had
even penned an article

00:30:15.810 --> 00:30:17.373
in his movement's newspaper,

00:30:17.373 --> 00:30:18.680
(foreign language)

00:30:18.680 --> 00:30:21.970
where he denounced antisemitism
in no uncertain terms.

00:30:21.970 --> 00:30:23.317
He wrote quote,

00:30:23.317 --> 00:30:25.957
"It is certainly abusive
to speak of a Jewish peril

00:30:25.957 --> 00:30:27.210
"in France."

00:30:27.210 --> 00:30:29.940
In particular, he
highlighted the way that Jews

00:30:29.940 --> 00:30:32.970
whose families had long resided in France

00:30:32.970 --> 00:30:36.550
should be assumed to be good citizens.

00:30:36.550 --> 00:30:39.537
These Jews, he wrote quote,
"Took part as soldiers,

00:30:39.537 --> 00:30:41.507
"as officers in the national wars.

00:30:41.507 --> 00:30:43.637
"They have mixed their blood
with that of the peasants,

00:30:43.637 --> 00:30:45.737
"the workers, the bourgeois of France.

00:30:45.737 --> 00:30:47.797
"They are French and
to want to exclude them

00:30:47.797 --> 00:30:49.007
"from the national community,

00:30:49.007 --> 00:30:51.587
"or even to deny their full
rights as French citizens

00:30:51.587 --> 00:30:54.407
"is to wish to weaken the
country that they have served

00:30:54.407 --> 00:30:56.457
"and that they should continue to serve."

00:30:57.480 --> 00:31:00.840
This column was reprinted in the bulletin

00:31:00.840 --> 00:31:03.330
of the Federation of Jewish
Societies of Algeria,

00:31:03.330 --> 00:31:05.510
the community's monthly newsletter.

00:31:05.510 --> 00:31:08.050
And given the level of
involvement of the Aboulker

00:31:08.050 --> 00:31:09.520
with community institutions,

00:31:09.520 --> 00:31:12.820
it is extremely likely that
many members of the family

00:31:12.820 --> 00:31:14.900
and those in the wider
milio of the insurgency

00:31:14.900 --> 00:31:17.530
would have read this article
and thus been familiar

00:31:17.530 --> 00:31:20.320
with the more progressive
term and royalist thinking

00:31:20.320 --> 00:31:21.573
regarding the Jews.

00:31:23.230 --> 00:31:25.700
The mention of Jewish
soldiers specifically here,

00:31:25.700 --> 00:31:27.840
was also hardly incidental.

00:31:27.840 --> 00:31:30.210
Even in an infamous
statement where he embraced

00:31:30.210 --> 00:31:33.310
Marshall Pétain and Vichy,
leading conservative resistor

00:31:33.310 --> 00:31:36.480
Alie Frene had answered the
question of who to recruit

00:31:36.480 --> 00:31:38.627
to the resistance by saying, quote,

00:31:38.627 --> 00:31:40.277
"French men of old extraction

00:31:40.277 --> 00:31:42.057
"to the exclusion of foreigners,

00:31:42.057 --> 00:31:44.067
"even those who are naturalized.

00:31:44.067 --> 00:31:46.937
"And Jews, if they really fought

00:31:46.937 --> 00:31:49.290
"in one of the two World Wars."

00:31:49.290 --> 00:31:51.340
A very high percentage
of the Jewish fighters

00:31:51.340 --> 00:31:53.470
in the Algiers insurrection
were veterans of the campaign

00:31:53.470 --> 00:31:56.460
of 1940, including José Aboulker himself,

00:31:56.460 --> 00:31:58.060
who had served as an army medic.

00:31:58.919 --> 00:32:02.070
José Aboulker would later
explain his close cooperation

00:32:02.070 --> 00:32:04.100
with d'Astier in simpler terms.

00:32:04.100 --> 00:32:05.730
Quote, "We had something in common

00:32:05.730 --> 00:32:08.837
"that the generations of today
no longer are familiar with,

00:32:08.837 --> 00:32:10.447
"and which is called patriotism,

00:32:10.447 --> 00:32:13.917
"which was a sentiment of a
force that no one could doubt.

00:32:13.917 --> 00:32:16.387
"But part of what appeared
to underlay this mutual sense

00:32:16.387 --> 00:32:19.887
"of patriotism was specifically
the devotion displays

00:32:19.887 --> 00:32:21.867
"on the battlefield Aboulker,

00:32:21.867 --> 00:32:23.887
"his father before in the World War I,

00:32:23.887 --> 00:32:26.427
"and so many of their
Algerian Jewish comrades."

00:32:28.510 --> 00:32:31.570
So to conclude the unlikely
alliance at the heart

00:32:31.570 --> 00:32:33.820
of the November 8th
insurrection between Jews

00:32:33.820 --> 00:32:36.120
and frequently anti-semitic
arch conservatives

00:32:36.120 --> 00:32:38.410
forces us to rethink
our conventional picture

00:32:38.410 --> 00:32:41.410
of who resisted and why
during the second World War

00:32:41.410 --> 00:32:42.940
and the Shoal.

00:32:42.940 --> 00:32:45.040
Admittedly, part of our misperception

00:32:45.040 --> 00:32:47.440
can be laid at the feet
of the post-war writings

00:32:47.440 --> 00:32:49.820
of the leading insurgents themselves.

00:32:49.820 --> 00:32:52.720
In 1946, when d'Astier submitted a list

00:32:52.720 --> 00:32:54.720
of those who participated
in the insurrection,

00:32:54.720 --> 00:32:57.460
he depicted himself as
their undisputed leader.

00:32:57.460 --> 00:32:59.260
And while he did include José Aboulker,

00:32:59.260 --> 00:33:03.550
he explicitly excluded hundreds
of others, mostly Jewish,

00:33:03.550 --> 00:33:06.640
who were now part of a Veterans
Association of November 8th,

00:33:06.640 --> 00:33:09.200
which he claimed was not to be confused

00:33:09.200 --> 00:33:11.690
with the resistance network itself.

00:33:11.690 --> 00:33:13.027
Likewise, Aboulker's own memoir

00:33:13.027 --> 00:33:15.540
while paying tribute to d'Astier,

00:33:15.540 --> 00:33:18.960
spoke about the broader
committee of five in acid terms,

00:33:18.960 --> 00:33:20.520
calling them a total failure,

00:33:20.520 --> 00:33:22.980
in contrast to the shock troops he had led

00:33:22.980 --> 00:33:25.650
and describing the
characteristics of the sincere,

00:33:25.650 --> 00:33:29.600
Vichysto-resistant as quote,
honorable and ineffective,

00:33:29.600 --> 00:33:31.430
while mocking the group more generally

00:33:31.430 --> 00:33:34.470
as by definition, indecisive.

00:33:34.470 --> 00:33:37.240
And yet nonetheless, it
was this rebel Alliance

00:33:37.240 --> 00:33:38.740
that made the Algiers underground

00:33:38.740 --> 00:33:42.500
once arguably the finest hour
of the Vichysto-resistant

00:33:42.500 --> 00:33:43.670
and strategically speaking,

00:33:43.670 --> 00:33:46.010
the most consequential
Jewish resistance movement

00:33:46.010 --> 00:33:47.417
of the second World War.

00:33:47.417 --> 00:33:50.273
Thank you.

00:33:50.273 --> 00:33:54.800
- Thank you, Ethan for that
was really fascinating.

00:33:54.800 --> 00:33:57.240
A story that I did not know much about,

00:33:57.240 --> 00:34:00.527
and I'm completely fascinated by it.

00:34:00.527 --> 00:34:02.570
And I personally have a lot of questions.

00:34:02.570 --> 00:34:05.060
I would encourage everyone in the audience

00:34:05.060 --> 00:34:10.020
to please submit questions
using the Q&amp;A function.

00:34:10.020 --> 00:34:13.170
We have a bunch mostly from Alice Kaplan,

00:34:13.170 --> 00:34:17.730
who is very eager, I know to,

00:34:17.730 --> 00:34:20.710
I will ventriloquist her questions,

00:34:20.710 --> 00:34:25.710
but first of all, a question
just a little background,

00:34:25.980 --> 00:34:29.280
I think might be helpful
for people listening.

00:34:29.280 --> 00:34:34.280
So at one point you did
mention that Jews were 10%

00:34:34.310 --> 00:34:37.110
of the population of Algiers.

00:34:37.110 --> 00:34:40.560
And I think that might surprise people.

00:34:40.560 --> 00:34:44.610
So if you could say a little
bit more about the demographics

00:34:44.610 --> 00:34:47.330
in Algeria and especially in the cities

00:34:47.330 --> 00:34:52.330
and also bringing in Muslims
and the relative population.

00:34:52.720 --> 00:34:57.720
- Yeah, so I mean, Algeria
broadly had 6 million,

00:34:58.500 --> 00:35:02.440
Muslims at this time, roughly
a million French settlers

00:35:02.440 --> 00:35:05.790
and 120,000 or so Jews.

00:35:05.790 --> 00:35:10.600
So they are 10% of the French
citizens broadly speaking

00:35:10.600 --> 00:35:11.433
in Algeria.

00:35:11.433 --> 00:35:14.760
It's so happens that
Algiers is substantially

00:35:14.760 --> 00:35:18.670
a European city in many ways by the 1930s.

00:35:18.670 --> 00:35:23.430
That is almost 70% of the
inhabitants are either settlers

00:35:23.430 --> 00:35:24.453
or Jews.

00:35:25.290 --> 00:35:30.290
I think it's about 9% Jewish,
60% settler, 30% Muslims.

00:35:31.450 --> 00:35:35.850
So yeah, I mean, the demographics
are such the Jews are,

00:35:35.850 --> 00:35:38.390
I mean, a whole another piece of the story

00:35:38.390 --> 00:35:41.890
is that Jews are seeking to regain

00:35:41.890 --> 00:35:44.870
of course, a position
of equal citizenship,

00:35:44.870 --> 00:35:48.160
and they are fighting off
the prospect of Nazi-ism,

00:35:48.160 --> 00:35:51.410
but there are also essentially
fighting to recover

00:35:51.410 --> 00:35:54.300
what remains a privileged
position in colonial society.

00:35:54.300 --> 00:35:58.680
There are extensive debates
about what Jews should do

00:35:58.680 --> 00:36:01.220
with regard to that very
question in the period

00:36:01.220 --> 00:36:03.690
after the landing, particularly
because it takes so long

00:36:03.690 --> 00:36:05.160
for citizenship to be restored.

00:36:05.160 --> 00:36:08.080
And there is pressure
from certain Muslim allies

00:36:08.080 --> 00:36:10.960
for them to pursue equal
citizenship for all,

00:36:10.960 --> 00:36:13.070
rather than simply for themselves.

00:36:13.070 --> 00:36:15.200
I'm happy to speak more about those.

00:36:15.200 --> 00:36:18.840
- Okay, all right, so here's
one of Alice's question.

00:36:18.840 --> 00:36:23.640
So all these Vichy guys had
they ever been in Algeria

00:36:23.640 --> 00:36:25.333
before 1942?

00:36:26.170 --> 00:36:29.400
Were they thinking about
Algeria and France?

00:36:29.400 --> 00:36:32.640
And the antisemites on the
far right on the ground

00:36:32.640 --> 00:36:37.640
in Algeria, were they much more
extreme than the Vichy guys?

00:36:38.930 --> 00:36:42.543
Were they like sinine level anti-semites?

00:36:43.980 --> 00:36:44.813
- Great questions.

00:36:44.813 --> 00:36:47.220
So, I mean, most of
these guys had not been

00:36:47.220 --> 00:36:48.070
in Algeria before.

00:36:48.070 --> 00:36:50.360
I mean, certainly not the
people in the Committee of Five,

00:36:50.360 --> 00:36:51.193
they go there.

00:36:51.193 --> 00:36:54.090
I mean, in many cases,
they go to already 1940

00:36:54.090 --> 00:36:57.600
and like, you can read
conflicting accounts

00:36:57.600 --> 00:36:58.820
of some of their motivations.

00:36:58.820 --> 00:37:02.910
Like le Mica Dubois is this
super successful businessman.

00:37:02.910 --> 00:37:06.710
And some people think that
he was very cynical in his

00:37:06.710 --> 00:37:09.580
connections to the Americans
and the Committee of Five,

00:37:09.580 --> 00:37:11.360
other people have more
charitable interpretations of him

00:37:11.360 --> 00:37:13.130
as a Patriot.

00:37:13.130 --> 00:37:15.710
But there's a series of business interests

00:37:15.710 --> 00:37:17.680
that lead certain people there.

00:37:17.680 --> 00:37:21.970
In some cases people go there
because they are compromised.

00:37:21.970 --> 00:37:26.080
d'Astier was in a resistance
network in France proper,

00:37:26.080 --> 00:37:29.270
and they escape to Algeria.

00:37:29.270 --> 00:37:31.420
But basically, I mean,
I shouldn't say that

00:37:31.420 --> 00:37:34.100
they've never been, I can't
say whether they ever visited

00:37:34.100 --> 00:37:35.690
Algeria previously, right.

00:37:35.690 --> 00:37:39.170
But they have no particular
history or connection

00:37:39.170 --> 00:37:40.130
to Algeria.

00:37:40.130 --> 00:37:42.670
So, yes, I mean, by and
large, I would say that

00:37:42.670 --> 00:37:46.710
these folks are anti-semitism
is less central for them,

00:37:46.710 --> 00:37:50.560
than it is for the ultras
of the settlor classes,

00:37:50.560 --> 00:37:54.210
which Alice, you know at least
as much about it as I do.

00:37:54.210 --> 00:37:57.130
And anti-semitism was really central

00:37:57.130 --> 00:37:58.623
to their political culture.

00:38:00.690 --> 00:38:03.430
Clearly there's a calculus that goes on.

00:38:03.430 --> 00:38:07.080
I try to explain some of
that calculus in my talk,

00:38:07.080 --> 00:38:10.130
where it's not that most of these folks

00:38:10.130 --> 00:38:12.210
who are the Vichysto-resistant
are necessarily

00:38:12.210 --> 00:38:14.630
that positively disposed toward Jews,

00:38:14.630 --> 00:38:17.993
but they are more focused
on re-igniting the war

00:38:17.993 --> 00:38:19.310
against the Germans.

00:38:19.310 --> 00:38:21.400
And we have to keep in mind,

00:38:21.400 --> 00:38:25.140
I mean, once we have that
agreement in the summer of 1942,

00:38:25.140 --> 00:38:26.660
between d'Astier and Aboulker,

00:38:26.660 --> 00:38:29.620
it's explicit that this is
for a finite period of time.

00:38:29.620 --> 00:38:31.920
I mean, they can, it's always easier

00:38:31.920 --> 00:38:34.650
to work with someone who you
are hardly disagree with,

00:38:34.650 --> 00:38:36.720
when you know you're going
to have a chance to hash out

00:38:36.720 --> 00:38:38.560
those disagreements later.

00:38:38.560 --> 00:38:40.453
So I think that's crucial as well.

00:38:42.680 --> 00:38:43.513
I think I answered it.

00:38:43.513 --> 00:38:46.700
- Yeah, so I wanted to
probe a little bit more

00:38:46.700 --> 00:38:51.700
about the Vichy resistance guys.

00:38:51.740 --> 00:38:53.990
And so listening to it,

00:38:53.990 --> 00:38:57.940
I couldn't help thinking
not to present ties,

00:38:57.940 --> 00:39:02.140
but I couldn't help thinking
about like the Lincoln Project,

00:39:02.140 --> 00:39:02.973
and different.

00:39:02.973 --> 00:39:06.650
I mean, so what, first
of all, what is really,

00:39:06.650 --> 00:39:10.170
I mean, is it about patriotism?

00:39:10.170 --> 00:39:14.160
Is it just about like this
idea that how can you side with

00:39:15.893 --> 00:39:16.910
the invader, the enemy,

00:39:16.910 --> 00:39:20.733
and if so, what does take them so long?

00:39:22.070 --> 00:39:24.270
When do they start to resist?

00:39:24.270 --> 00:39:27.550
I mean, it's not Milton is not until 1943.

00:39:27.550 --> 00:39:31.210
So is that how much of that
is waiting to see which way

00:39:31.210 --> 00:39:34.320
the wind was blowing,
which way the war would go?

00:39:34.320 --> 00:39:35.153
- They're good questions.

00:39:35.153 --> 00:39:37.306
I mean, they're not one group, right?

00:39:37.306 --> 00:39:40.610
Those that have been put under
this rubric by historians

00:39:40.610 --> 00:39:41.443
in recent years.

00:39:41.443 --> 00:39:45.310
So there are those who actually
are very early to the game

00:39:45.310 --> 00:39:47.740
in a way that is shocking to us today,

00:39:47.740 --> 00:39:48.690
because the way that we've aligned

00:39:48.690 --> 00:39:51.653
extreme right of the
thirties with ardent Vichyism

00:39:51.653 --> 00:39:52.486
in the forties.

00:39:52.486 --> 00:39:55.210
But some of those folks
in the early months

00:39:55.210 --> 00:39:58.047
are already saying, "Well,
the Marshal can't resist.

00:39:58.047 --> 00:39:59.410
"We gotta do it for him."

00:39:59.410 --> 00:40:02.530
And so some of them are
not at all latecomers.

00:40:02.530 --> 00:40:05.250
Then you have people like
Milton who evolve in some way,

00:40:05.250 --> 00:40:07.660
whether you want to say
that evolution is purely

00:40:07.660 --> 00:40:09.670
kinda cynical and self-serving,

00:40:09.670 --> 00:40:12.760
or what do you want to
say that they realize.

00:40:12.760 --> 00:40:15.950
I mean, there are certainly folks also

00:40:15.950 --> 00:40:20.900
who are loyalists to Vichy
without being active resistors,

00:40:20.900 --> 00:40:23.240
partly because they assume the Marshall

00:40:23.240 --> 00:40:24.900
is acting on their behalf

00:40:24.900 --> 00:40:27.170
and they come to conclude
over time that he is not,

00:40:27.170 --> 00:40:29.910
and they then become
disillusioned with the regime

00:40:29.910 --> 00:40:32.410
and become resistors.

00:40:32.410 --> 00:40:35.360
But I think patriotism is the heart of it.

00:40:35.360 --> 00:40:40.360
I mean, I think that there
are people who just feel very,

00:40:41.430 --> 00:40:43.160
they feel very strongly
against the Germans.

00:40:43.160 --> 00:40:46.900
They feel ultimately like
they have to defend France

00:40:46.900 --> 00:40:51.260
and that's sort of their
kind of singular focus

00:40:51.260 --> 00:40:52.730
in the early months there.

00:40:52.730 --> 00:40:57.070
And in a way it maybe isn't
that surprising on reflection

00:40:57.070 --> 00:41:00.080
that some of the same extreme
right guys from the thirties

00:41:00.080 --> 00:41:02.900
are some of the earliest to want to resist

00:41:02.900 --> 00:41:03.990
within the Vichy circles,

00:41:03.990 --> 00:41:06.380
because they're used to being active

00:41:06.380 --> 00:41:09.320
in kind of radical politics
and their radical politics

00:41:09.320 --> 00:41:13.650
has its own kind of ardent
patriotic nationalism attached

00:41:13.650 --> 00:41:15.337
to it already before the war.

00:41:16.340 --> 00:41:17.710
- Great, okay.

00:41:17.710 --> 00:41:22.710
So questions I'm seeing here
about Muslims and about,

00:41:24.020 --> 00:41:26.010
so if you could say a little bit more

00:41:26.010 --> 00:41:28.900
about Muslim resistance here,

00:41:28.900 --> 00:41:32.020
and also a question from
someone in the audience

00:41:32.020 --> 00:41:35.240
who wants you to clarify
the use of the term Muslim.

00:41:35.240 --> 00:41:39.210
So are you referring to
a mostly Arabized elite

00:41:39.210 --> 00:41:42.960
or the Amazi communities or both and yeah.

00:41:42.960 --> 00:41:45.092
And if you could say more about their

00:41:45.092 --> 00:41:47.090
role in this resistance.

00:41:47.090 --> 00:41:49.330
- Yeah, so I mean the role of Muslims

00:41:49.330 --> 00:41:52.650
and I would use that term to describe,

00:41:52.650 --> 00:41:54.780
just as I would in a
parallel way to the way

00:41:54.780 --> 00:41:56.397
that I would use the term Jews.

00:41:56.397 --> 00:41:58.220
And I'll talk a little bit
about this in my first book.

00:41:58.220 --> 00:42:01.940
I mean, I think there
were and are in many ways

00:42:01.940 --> 00:42:05.270
to be in some way connected to Muslimness,

00:42:05.270 --> 00:42:07.430
for some people that
is Islam as a religion

00:42:07.430 --> 00:42:09.300
and for other people
it's much more cultural,

00:42:09.300 --> 00:42:11.640
and that certainly was true in Algeria.

00:42:11.640 --> 00:42:13.440
The category of Muslim was racialized

00:42:13.440 --> 00:42:15.480
by the French administration,

00:42:15.480 --> 00:42:18.379
such that it did not distinguish
between religious practice

00:42:18.379 --> 00:42:21.683
or lack of practice at all and
it was all based on descent.

00:42:22.570 --> 00:42:25.110
But the reality was a very large spectrum.

00:42:25.110 --> 00:42:28.730
So to me, yeah, I mean I,

00:42:28.730 --> 00:42:31.740
there were various Muslim political groups

00:42:31.740 --> 00:42:33.846
and we can talk a little
bit more about that.

00:42:33.846 --> 00:42:38.120
There were very few Muslims
in this resistance movement.

00:42:38.120 --> 00:42:40.140
If there were some
resisters during the war,

00:42:40.140 --> 00:42:42.170
the two most common avenues

00:42:42.170 --> 00:42:45.420
are aligned with the
Algerian Communist Party

00:42:45.420 --> 00:42:48.510
and then joining the liberation armies,

00:42:48.510 --> 00:42:51.930
as they begin to fight their
way up into France, right?

00:42:51.930 --> 00:42:54.220
That's the vast majority
of Muslim Algerians

00:42:54.220 --> 00:42:56.020
who joined the resistance in some form,

00:42:56.020 --> 00:42:58.800
but there are interesting exceptions.

00:42:58.800 --> 00:43:01.100
And the most interesting, I
have a whole chapter about him

00:43:01.100 --> 00:43:05.120
in the book is a man named
Muhammad Abdul Azis Kasus,

00:43:05.120 --> 00:43:08.790
who is very closely aligned
with a certain movement

00:43:08.790 --> 00:43:10.110
in Algeria, led by

00:43:10.110 --> 00:43:10.943
(foreign language)

00:43:10.943 --> 00:43:14.010
which is sort of a reformist
movement that is increasingly

00:43:14.010 --> 00:43:15.870
moving toward nationalism.

00:43:15.870 --> 00:43:18.490
And because Kasus is
actually the primary author

00:43:18.490 --> 00:43:21.060
of a famous document from during the war,

00:43:21.060 --> 00:43:23.713
the manifest of the Algerian People,

00:43:24.610 --> 00:43:28.890
which comes out in 1943, in March of 1943.

00:43:28.890 --> 00:43:32.830
And in that manifestt, it actually says,

00:43:32.830 --> 00:43:36.310
given the repeal of the Crémieux Decree,

00:43:36.310 --> 00:43:39.620
Algeria and Muslims are led to wonder

00:43:39.620 --> 00:43:42.310
if French citizenship is worth much less

00:43:42.310 --> 00:43:44.760
than it would be to be
an Algerian citizen.

00:43:44.760 --> 00:43:47.660
So there are certain muscles
like that who actually talk

00:43:47.660 --> 00:43:50.170
very actively about the connection

00:43:50.170 --> 00:43:52.270
between what goes on
with Jews during the war

00:43:52.270 --> 00:43:55.290
and how they are looking for
new political alignments,

00:43:55.290 --> 00:43:57.150
including an alliance as I referred to

00:43:57.150 --> 00:44:01.500
between Muslims and Jews
to fight for equal rights.

00:44:01.500 --> 00:44:03.980
And there are a handful of other
Muslims who are referred to

00:44:03.980 --> 00:44:07.500
in various accounts of the
uprising who participated

00:44:07.500 --> 00:44:09.700
in different groups, for sure.

00:44:09.700 --> 00:44:14.080
But there were also those in
the movement who were worried

00:44:14.080 --> 00:44:18.330
about the intensity of access
propaganda Visa de Muslims,

00:44:18.330 --> 00:44:22.700
and therefore were hesitant
to invite Muslims to join.

00:44:22.700 --> 00:44:27.700
I think, broadly speaking,
this was ultimately a fight

00:44:29.540 --> 00:44:32.220
to throw off the Germans,
and for many Jews

00:44:32.220 --> 00:44:34.120
to regain their citizenship.

00:44:34.120 --> 00:44:37.730
It wasn't a fight that
necessarily clearly implicated

00:44:37.730 --> 00:44:39.790
Muslim political activists

00:44:39.790 --> 00:44:41.690
for some of the reasons I've already said.

00:44:41.690 --> 00:44:42.850
- Okay, great.

00:44:42.850 --> 00:44:46.030
So here's a question from David Sorkin.

00:44:46.030 --> 00:44:50.660
He says that Vichy's
Jewish statutes of 1941

00:44:50.660 --> 00:44:53.600
included exemptions
for Jews who had fought

00:44:53.600 --> 00:44:56.800
in either World War or whose
families had been in France

00:44:56.800 --> 00:44:58.440
for five generations.

00:44:58.440 --> 00:44:59.960
So in what sense could you say

00:44:59.960 --> 00:45:02.060
that the monarchist reactionary figures

00:45:02.060 --> 00:45:05.290
in the uprising are
actually acting in line with

00:45:05.290 --> 00:45:08.760
a certain understanding of Vichy policy?

00:45:08.760 --> 00:45:12.040
- Yeah, great question as
usual, thank you, David.

00:45:12.040 --> 00:45:16.130
So yeah, I mean, I actually
thought of mentioning that.

00:45:16.130 --> 00:45:21.130
Clearly there's a broader
way in which military service

00:45:22.240 --> 00:45:26.370
is honored by Vichy, including
to a significant extent

00:45:26.370 --> 00:45:27.730
for Jews.

00:45:27.730 --> 00:45:31.870
You have all these petitions
to Vichy that many of us

00:45:31.870 --> 00:45:35.980
have seen from right after
the first of Jewish statute

00:45:35.980 --> 00:45:39.437
where people say, "My
husband or my father served

00:45:39.437 --> 00:45:41.480
"in World War I and you should
make an exception for him."

00:45:41.480 --> 00:45:45.240
Now, while most of those are not honored,

00:45:45.240 --> 00:45:49.210
it's a reflection partly
already of the cultural ethos

00:45:49.210 --> 00:45:50.736
around wartime service.

00:45:50.736 --> 00:45:54.070
And then as David said, there
are these exemptions in 1941.

00:45:54.070 --> 00:45:58.290
So yeah, I mean, I think
that it does reflect that.

00:45:58.290 --> 00:46:02.200
I think, one of the other
things I talk about in the book

00:46:02.200 --> 00:46:07.000
is that a kind of effort to regain manhood

00:46:07.000 --> 00:46:11.840
is one of the things that goes
on in this Jewish insurgency.

00:46:11.840 --> 00:46:15.920
And you have, you saw
briefly the images there,

00:46:15.920 --> 00:46:19.100
you have a boxing ring as the
center for the largest force

00:46:19.100 --> 00:46:20.610
within the insurgency.

00:46:20.610 --> 00:46:22.930
You have like famous boxers
coming through there,

00:46:22.930 --> 00:46:25.050
you have fencing, which,

00:46:25.050 --> 00:46:26.770
however strange it may seem to us today

00:46:26.770 --> 00:46:29.330
was very strongly associated
with European manhood

00:46:29.330 --> 00:46:30.163
at this time.

00:46:30.163 --> 00:46:32.520
And Jews had been
disproportionately participating

00:46:32.520 --> 00:46:34.230
in fencing for decades.

00:46:34.230 --> 00:46:36.610
Get a lot of fencing
competitions, had Jewish finalists

00:46:36.610 --> 00:46:38.740
who were in the fencing
competitions in Algeria,

00:46:38.740 --> 00:46:41.560
in the early 40s, despite the
opposition of anti-Semites.

00:46:41.560 --> 00:46:43.990
She had all of this sort
of hyper masculine energy

00:46:43.990 --> 00:46:46.080
and many of these people were veterans,

00:46:46.080 --> 00:46:47.780
as I said of the campaign in 1940.

00:46:47.780 --> 00:46:50.860
So in some ways I think all
of this is kind of connected

00:46:52.333 --> 00:46:55.500
that their efforts to
reclaim masculinity comes

00:46:55.500 --> 00:46:58.250
partly in the form of
joining a resistance group.

00:46:58.250 --> 00:47:02.970
And they are more palatable
to certain rightists

00:47:02.970 --> 00:47:05.900
because of the fact that they connect to,

00:47:05.900 --> 00:47:08.053
military background, military culture.

00:47:09.130 --> 00:47:12.550
- So to follow up on that
question, there's all this,

00:47:12.550 --> 00:47:14.760
you're describing this
sort of masculine energy,

00:47:14.760 --> 00:47:17.670
it's this story about reclaiming
mass masculine identity,

00:47:17.670 --> 00:47:20.850
but what about women in
these resistance groups?

00:47:20.850 --> 00:47:24.830
You mentioned Colette, the
sister of José, I think,

00:47:24.830 --> 00:47:27.670
but are, were there other women involved?

00:47:27.670 --> 00:47:30.330
- There were other women
and Colette is fascinating

00:47:30.330 --> 00:47:34.330
and I'm actually, I'm
starting the book with Colette

00:47:34.330 --> 00:47:39.330
because she wrote a five
volume memoir of her childhood.

00:47:39.840 --> 00:47:44.553
She later became a very
kind of illustrious healer

00:47:45.990 --> 00:47:50.360
through psychological work in Israel.

00:47:50.360 --> 00:47:53.290
And so she was a deeply spiritual person

00:47:53.290 --> 00:47:55.460
and that's part of what
punctuates her memoir,

00:47:55.460 --> 00:47:59.400
but she also shows how
much she felt the burden

00:47:59.400 --> 00:48:00.652
of her family's history.

00:48:00.652 --> 00:48:01.485
I didn't have time to get into it here,

00:48:01.485 --> 00:48:05.380
but her family had this
kind of rabbinic dynasty

00:48:05.380 --> 00:48:06.213
in its history.

00:48:06.213 --> 00:48:08.130
It had, then all these people who had been

00:48:08.130 --> 00:48:11.000
the first Jew to practice
medicine and Algiers,

00:48:11.000 --> 00:48:12.680
people who were enormously successful

00:48:12.680 --> 00:48:15.000
in secular colonial society.

00:48:15.000 --> 00:48:17.610
And so she hears things from family

00:48:17.610 --> 00:48:18.837
and she says things like,

00:48:18.837 --> 00:48:22.547
"I understood that I would
be the one in my generation

00:48:22.547 --> 00:48:25.847
"to help save the Jewish people,
maybe to save the world."

00:48:26.750 --> 00:48:27.800
So she's fascinating.

00:48:27.800 --> 00:48:29.100
And she plays a really important role.

00:48:29.100 --> 00:48:30.390
I mean, her father also describes

00:48:30.390 --> 00:48:33.090
how she kept everything
together in the house,

00:48:33.090 --> 00:48:34.750
when everything's buzzing
and there's a million people

00:48:34.750 --> 00:48:37.390
coming through and she's basically

00:48:37.390 --> 00:48:39.310
keeping all the trains running.

00:48:39.310 --> 00:48:41.430
There are, and there
are several other women

00:48:41.430 --> 00:48:44.919
who maybe we would say have
comparable roles of the wife,

00:48:44.919 --> 00:48:46.424
(foreign language)

00:48:46.424 --> 00:48:49.290
She like, there's accounts
about how she's making food

00:48:49.290 --> 00:48:51.240
for all of these people on
the night of the uprising.

00:48:51.240 --> 00:48:53.990
And she's hiding guns in
different places in the house.

00:48:54.910 --> 00:48:59.610
It's clearly a small number
of women who participate

00:48:59.610 --> 00:49:03.180
and we even have an account of a one

00:49:04.210 --> 00:49:06.160
altercation a little bit on
the night of the uprising,

00:49:06.160 --> 00:49:10.610
where certain male resisters
don't want women taking part,

00:49:10.610 --> 00:49:12.810
which I think reinforces the sense

00:49:12.810 --> 00:49:17.030
of a kind of hyper masculine
identity for certain segments.

00:49:17.030 --> 00:49:19.550
But there were women who
played important roles,

00:49:19.550 --> 00:49:22.320
certainly particularly Colette Aboulker.

00:49:22.320 --> 00:49:23.153
- Great, okay.

00:49:23.153 --> 00:49:25.230
Another question from Alice Kaplin,

00:49:25.230 --> 00:49:29.510
she's wondering what you have to say about

00:49:29.510 --> 00:49:33.980
the reluctance of the allies
to cancel the abrogation

00:49:33.980 --> 00:49:35.890
of the Crémieux Decree.

00:49:35.890 --> 00:49:37.840
So the Jews had to wait for months

00:49:37.840 --> 00:49:39.630
to get their citizenship back.

00:49:39.630 --> 00:49:40.530
How do we explain that?

00:49:40.530 --> 00:49:42.990
Is that American anti-semitism at work

00:49:42.990 --> 00:49:45.960
or is it the fault of the French, what?

00:49:45.960 --> 00:49:48.943
- Well, I mean, it's a complex story.

00:49:49.930 --> 00:49:52.890
I think the Americans were persuaded

00:49:52.890 --> 00:49:54.810
and Robert Murphy writes
about this in his memoir

00:49:54.810 --> 00:49:56.560
in ways that are frankly
embarrassing at this point.

00:49:56.560 --> 00:50:00.408
But he felt very strongly that,

00:50:00.408 --> 00:50:03.420
the Americans were very worried

00:50:03.420 --> 00:50:05.450
that there would be a lot of Muslim anger

00:50:05.450 --> 00:50:08.320
if Jewish citizenship was restored.

00:50:08.320 --> 00:50:11.560
There is intense lobbying from
the American Jewish community

00:50:11.560 --> 00:50:12.410
that takes place

00:50:12.410 --> 00:50:14.660
and that ultimately has
a significant impact.

00:50:16.250 --> 00:50:18.030
And people are miffed and Murphy says,

00:50:18.030 --> 00:50:20.950
they didn't understand how
everything was so different

00:50:20.950 --> 00:50:21.783
in North Africa.

00:50:21.783 --> 00:50:23.120
North African Jews are different,

00:50:23.120 --> 00:50:25.330
North African society is different.

00:50:25.330 --> 00:50:28.900
But there definitely were
people were persuaded that

00:50:28.900 --> 00:50:33.170
Jewish-Muslim enmity was primordial

00:50:33.170 --> 00:50:35.100
and that if Jews were given
back their citizenship,

00:50:35.100 --> 00:50:38.530
despite the fact that then
Jews produced letters, right,

00:50:38.530 --> 00:50:43.047
from leading Muslim city
counselors and figures saying,

00:50:43.047 --> 00:50:45.780
"We didn't have any joy about the

00:50:45.780 --> 00:50:47.630
abrogation of the Crémieux Decree

00:50:47.630 --> 00:50:52.030
and that that's not something
we celebrated at all.

00:50:52.030 --> 00:50:56.870
So but, so that's clearly a
factor then you I think have

00:50:56.870 --> 00:50:59.700
folks who never, I mean, you
have a significant segment

00:50:59.700 --> 00:51:02.570
of Algerian colonial society
that had been campaigning

00:51:02.570 --> 00:51:05.400
for the abrogation of
Crémieux Decree for 70 years.

00:51:05.400 --> 00:51:08.050
And so was deeply invested in that.

00:51:08.050 --> 00:51:11.872
And to some extent of
people like Henri Giraud,

00:51:11.872 --> 00:51:16.240
who's the governor general
for awhile after the landing.

00:51:16.240 --> 00:51:19.640
They are kind of responding to
the pressure from those folks

00:51:19.640 --> 00:51:20.777
and some of those folks.

00:51:20.777 --> 00:51:23.370
And some of the other Vichy
officials are also saying,

00:51:23.370 --> 00:51:25.490
there'll be a civil war between
the Jews and the Muslims.

00:51:25.490 --> 00:51:27.460
So there's a lot of that.

00:51:27.460 --> 00:51:31.130
But I also think that
the story I told today,

00:51:31.130 --> 00:51:32.890
is an important ingredient.

00:51:32.890 --> 00:51:37.020
That is the Vichysto-resistant,
are basically,

00:51:37.020 --> 00:51:40.860
like the slates wiped
clean in November, 1942.

00:51:40.860 --> 00:51:44.850
They and many of their supporters,

00:51:44.850 --> 00:51:48.520
wanna kind of rechart what
colonial Algeria looks like.

00:51:48.520 --> 00:51:51.540
Jews are fighting for a different
vision of colonial Algeria

00:51:51.540 --> 00:51:53.640
that aligns with their Republican Judaism.

00:51:54.484 --> 00:51:56.180
And so it's not shocking in that way

00:51:56.180 --> 00:51:59.900
that given that they had
no ideological consensus

00:51:59.900 --> 00:52:01.920
and that these two
visions were so opposed,

00:52:01.920 --> 00:52:04.110
it's not shocking that it
took effectively months

00:52:04.110 --> 00:52:05.330
to hash that out.

00:52:05.330 --> 00:52:07.880
And it's inseparable from the struggle

00:52:07.880 --> 00:52:10.520
between the Jihadist forces
and the godless forces

00:52:10.520 --> 00:52:12.053
in Algeria in 1943.

00:52:13.140 --> 00:52:17.420
- Great, okay, I'm going to
ask a selfish question here

00:52:17.420 --> 00:52:18.990
and I'd like to,

00:52:18.990 --> 00:52:21.830
yeah, thank you for mentioning my book

00:52:21.830 --> 00:52:24.830
and I, so I was very interested,

00:52:24.830 --> 00:52:29.140
I'm very interested in how
anti-Semitism becomes a key part

00:52:29.140 --> 00:52:31.137
of right wing ideology in France.

00:52:31.137 --> 00:52:34.690
And so part of what I was
interested in was looking at

00:52:34.690 --> 00:52:36.590
a possible origin point for that

00:52:36.590 --> 00:52:39.570
or one of the possible origin points.

00:52:39.570 --> 00:52:42.827
But we know that like something,

00:52:42.827 --> 00:52:47.460
we normally think of World War
II is sort of the culmination

00:52:47.460 --> 00:52:48.420
of that right.

00:52:48.420 --> 00:52:53.420
Vichy is the culmination, it's
the revenge on for Dreyfus.

00:52:54.360 --> 00:52:56.520
And they're able to enact,

00:52:56.520 --> 00:53:01.000
to really make antisemitism
a part of state policy.

00:53:01.000 --> 00:53:04.760
But you're kind of giving
this other possible other

00:53:04.760 --> 00:53:05.990
way to see it.

00:53:05.990 --> 00:53:08.190
And then it, maybe it's a culmination,

00:53:08.190 --> 00:53:11.140
but it's also things go over the hill

00:53:11.140 --> 00:53:15.070
and it's maybe also the end
or an end point for that.

00:53:15.070 --> 00:53:18.570
I don't know, how do you see that in?

00:53:18.570 --> 00:53:22.519
'Cause it's true that
anti-semitism stops being a kind of

00:53:22.519 --> 00:53:27.010
the key part of right wing
ideology after World War II,

00:53:27.010 --> 00:53:30.080
partly because it's discredited by Hitler,

00:53:30.080 --> 00:53:33.470
but maybe there's also
something else going on too.

00:53:33.470 --> 00:53:34.570
- Well, I mean,

00:53:34.570 --> 00:53:36.720
so I'm still learning
a lot about monarchists

00:53:36.720 --> 00:53:41.720
and 20th century France an
understudied subject for sure.

00:53:43.040 --> 00:53:45.600
But what I can, what I've gathered is,

00:53:45.600 --> 00:53:47.210
you have the Action française,

00:53:47.210 --> 00:53:49.130
which is this Neo-monachist organization,

00:53:49.130 --> 00:53:52.540
but of course they attract
many folks who are not

00:53:52.540 --> 00:53:55.560
monarchists per se, not the
d'Astier style of monarchist,

00:53:55.560 --> 00:53:57.360
where like your father
and your grandfather,

00:53:57.360 --> 00:53:59.600
and your great-grandfather were
monarchist for generations,

00:53:59.600 --> 00:54:00.980
but people who are basically

00:54:00.980 --> 00:54:02.650
interested in right wing radical politics.

00:54:02.650 --> 00:54:05.370
And Charles Maurras is
arguably the most influential,

00:54:05.370 --> 00:54:09.380
right-wing radical thinker
in 20th century, France.

00:54:09.380 --> 00:54:12.530
So that's like a different
brand of monarchism,

00:54:12.530 --> 00:54:15.690
but it becomes discredited effectively

00:54:15.690 --> 00:54:17.270
by a lot of the traditional monarchists

00:54:17.270 --> 00:54:18.680
by the 20s and 30s, right.

00:54:18.680 --> 00:54:21.930
There were announced by the
Holy See, I think in 1927,

00:54:21.930 --> 00:54:23.928
and then they're renounced by

00:54:23.928 --> 00:54:24.950
(foreign language)

00:54:24.950 --> 00:54:25.800
in the mid 30s.

00:54:25.800 --> 00:54:28.160
And we should point out, I mean,
it's a complicated history,

00:54:28.160 --> 00:54:31.770
but because of the
Bourbons, the legitimists,

00:54:31.770 --> 00:54:34.170
who are traditionally the
more conservative ones,

00:54:34.170 --> 00:54:38.720
were stuck as it were with a
Spanish line from the 1880s,

00:54:38.720 --> 00:54:39.553
(foreign language)

00:54:39.553 --> 00:54:42.390
becomes the defacto pretender
kind of for everybody,

00:54:42.390 --> 00:54:43.990
even though he's from
the only on East branch.

00:54:43.990 --> 00:54:46.358
But perhaps a consequence
of that is that the

00:54:46.358 --> 00:54:47.191
(foreign language)

00:54:47.191 --> 00:54:49.653
is always more moderate and up,

00:54:50.627 --> 00:54:52.830
he ends up sort of pushing things

00:54:52.830 --> 00:54:55.300
in a more moderate direction.

00:54:55.300 --> 00:54:59.130
Yeah, I mean, I think as anti-semitism,

00:54:59.130 --> 00:55:02.420
I think we could say that as anti-semitism

00:55:02.420 --> 00:55:05.860
becomes radicalized in
the 30s and early 40s,

00:55:05.860 --> 00:55:09.760
it becomes much more uncomfortable
for certain monarchists

00:55:09.760 --> 00:55:10.920
who are more traditionalist.

00:55:10.920 --> 00:55:13.390
- Yeah, okay, good,
that's super interesting.

00:55:13.390 --> 00:55:15.310
Okay, we're almost out of time,

00:55:15.310 --> 00:55:19.970
but I wanted to ask one
other question about

00:55:20.950 --> 00:55:25.950
why more Algerian Jews who were
expelled from their schools

00:55:26.320 --> 00:55:30.040
in 1940, faced all these
anti-semitic prosecutions.

00:55:30.040 --> 00:55:34.633
Why didn't more aside
with the FLN in the 50s.

00:55:35.850 --> 00:55:36.683
What do you think?

00:55:36.683 --> 00:55:37.780
How do you explain that?

00:55:37.780 --> 00:55:39.063
- Great question, right.

00:55:40.082 --> 00:55:43.003
It's a sort of a $64,000
question about Algerian history.

00:55:44.450 --> 00:55:47.130
Yeah, I mean, I think that in some ways

00:55:47.130 --> 00:55:51.120
there's a parallel between, if you will,

00:55:51.120 --> 00:55:56.120
1900 in the French main land
where the Dreyfus Affair

00:55:56.680 --> 00:56:00.560
is almost forgotten and seen
as, okay the Republic works,

00:56:00.560 --> 00:56:04.160
eventually Dreyfus was
pardoned and then of course

00:56:04.160 --> 00:56:06.240
he was exonerated 1906.

00:56:06.240 --> 00:56:09.200
There's a parallel in some
ways between that and 1945

00:56:09.200 --> 00:56:10.530
in Algeria.

00:56:10.530 --> 00:56:12.840
I mean, to some extent in
the French mainland as well,

00:56:12.840 --> 00:56:17.070
but basically the Vichy
years are in a way,

00:56:17.070 --> 00:56:18.720
I mean, they're not entirely forgotten.

00:56:18.720 --> 00:56:23.140
And so you have the attempt
of the FLN during the 50s

00:56:23.140 --> 00:56:26.300
repeatedly to invoke
the Vichy years and say,

00:56:26.300 --> 00:56:29.090
the same people who are
advocating for colonialism

00:56:29.090 --> 00:56:32.250
are the ones who, took
away your citizenship

00:56:32.250 --> 00:56:33.257
and treated you horribly then

00:56:33.257 --> 00:56:36.163
and we were your, we were
in solidarity with you.

00:56:37.050 --> 00:56:41.340
But in a certain way, it's
like the Jews basically just,

00:56:41.340 --> 00:56:43.700
kind of wanna paper that over

00:56:43.700 --> 00:56:45.910
and think that the real France,

00:56:45.910 --> 00:56:48.213
was the France that restored their rights.

00:56:49.160 --> 00:56:53.760
And they just, they also see
themselves, they're articulate,

00:56:53.760 --> 00:56:58.040
they see themselves as so
Frenchified by the 50s,

00:56:58.040 --> 00:57:00.740
that in a way it's almost
like there's no going back.

00:57:00.740 --> 00:57:03.370
- So they buy into the
godless myth in a sense

00:57:03.370 --> 00:57:04.340
and then yeah.

00:57:04.340 --> 00:57:06.443
- You saying of the resistors?

00:57:06.443 --> 00:57:08.950
- No, no, no the post-war Gaullist myth,

00:57:08.950 --> 00:57:11.630
yes, that everyone had
resisted that that wasn't

00:57:11.630 --> 00:57:14.790
the real France that had
done this to them and---

00:57:14.790 --> 00:57:16.970
- Yeah, but I think also they just,

00:57:16.970 --> 00:57:21.890
they see themselves as products
of a process of successful

00:57:21.890 --> 00:57:24.089
emancipation and Frenchification

00:57:24.089 --> 00:57:28.130
and they see Muslims as like
on the same track they hope,

00:57:28.130 --> 00:57:30.610
just several steps behind.

00:57:30.610 --> 00:57:33.990
And they kinda carry that
vision through to the end.

00:57:33.990 --> 00:57:36.950
- All right, well, we are
unfortunately out of time,

00:57:36.950 --> 00:57:40.160
but I wanna thank you for
this really enlightening

00:57:40.160 --> 00:57:44.430
and just fascinating presentation
and thanks for sharing it

00:57:44.430 --> 00:57:46.850
and co-hosting this event with us.

00:57:46.850 --> 00:57:49.040
So we're really looking
forward to the book.

00:57:49.040 --> 00:57:52.520
So I know everyone else is
applauding at home but---

00:57:53.540 --> 00:57:54.590
- Thanks for all the questions.

00:57:54.590 --> 00:57:55.423
- Yeah.

